- Reason to buy: {{slot:reason_to_buy_1}}
- Buy details: {{slot:buy_details_1}}
- Reason to sell: {{slot:reason_to_sell_1}}
- Sell details: {{slot:sell_details_1}}

Write a trading algorithm that implements exactly the strategies below. Evaluate every rule once per daily bar, after the close, and do not add, remove or reinterpret any rule.

- Strategy A (trades SPY):
{{slot:strategy_a}}
- Strategy B (trades QQQ):
{{slot:strategy_b}}

Return only the complete program.

Write a trading algorithm for SPY options that implements exactly the strategy below. Evaluate the rules on completed 15-minute bars, and do not add, remove or reinterpret any rule.

{{slot:strategy}}

Return only the complete program.

PARALLEL template: both slots run independently at the same time.

Slot 1:
{{slot:first}}

Slot 2:
{{slot:second}}

RACE template: on every bar, check each slot's reason to buy in slot order. The first slot whose reason holds takes sole ownership and carries out its buy details; the other slots may not act while it owns the template. Ownership ends when that slot's position is closed, and the race re-opens on the next bar.

Slot 1:
{{slot:first}}

Slot 2:
{{slot:second}}

SEQUENCE template: one slot is eligible at a time, starting with slot 1. A slot passes eligibility to the next slot after it opens and then closes a position. After the last slot, eligibility returns to slot 1.

Slot 1:
{{slot:first}}

Slot 2:
{{slot:second}}

STATE-GATED template: its slots may act only while the gate condition holds. On the bar the condition stops holding, close every position inside the template and reset its state.

Gate condition for this composition: {{condition}}

Slot 1:
{{slot:first}}

Slot 2:
{{slot:second}}

EVENT-GATED template: when its event condition becomes true (true today, false yesterday), the template is armed for the next m trading days, starting tomorrow. While armed, its slots may act. When the window ends, close every position inside the template and reset its state. A new event while armed restarts the window.

Event condition for this composition: {{condition}}
Arming window m = {{m}} trading days.

Slot 1:
{{slot:first}}

Slot 2:
{{slot:second}}

